    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "\nDNG is proud to present 29 Northbrook Avenue, Ranelagh, Dublin 6 to the market.\nThe bright and spacious accommodation extends to approximately 102sqm /\n1,098qft and briefly comprises of an entrance hallway, living room, kitchen, utility\nroom, a guest w.c completes the accommodation downstairs. Upstairs, there is a\nfamily bathroom and three spacious double bedrooms with the master bedroom\nbenefitting from an ensuite. No. 29 is further enhanced by the low maintenance\nprivate rear garden which is perfect spot for al fresco dining. \n\nNorthbrook Avenue is prized for its quiet residential character while remaining\nmoments from the vibrancy of Ranelagh village. Renowned cafés, restaurants and\nindependent shops are within walking distance, as is the LUAS, providing direct and\nconvenient access to the city centre. St Stephen's Green, Grafton Street and\nRathmines are all close by, and the area is exceptionally well served by Dublin's\nleading junior and senior schools, as well as major universities and colleges. It has\nthe added bonus of having direct gated access to a private walkway leading to the\npark at Ranelagh gardens and directly to Ranelagh village. There are several well-\nknown primary and secondary schools in the area including Scoil Bhríde; the first\never Gaelscoil in Ireland, Ranelagh Multi-Denominational School, Muckross College,\nGonzaga College, St Marys College and Sandford Park School. The area is also\nserviced by the Green LUAS Line and several bus routes. St. Stephen's Green is c.\n1.5km from the property, which is an approximate 20-minute walk. \n\nViewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
